---
layout: null
sitemap:
  exclude: true
---
{% comment %}
  Search index. Two bugs fixed:

  1. `"content": {{ page.content | jsonify }}` sat inside a `for post in site.posts`
     loop. `page` there is search.json itself, so every post entry carried this file's
     own body instead of the post's — the index was unusable for content matching.
  2. The pages loop emitted `{ }` for any page without a title, leaving empty objects
     and a trailing comma in the array. Untitled pages are now skipped outright.

  Content is truncated: the index is fetched on every visit to /search/, and shipping
  every full article would make it heavier than the pages it searches.
{% endcomment %}
[
  {% comment %}
    Index and listing pages are excluded. Their body text is a concatenation of every
    post title, category name and tag on the site, so they matched almost any query and
    outranked nothing useful — searching "jjimjilbang" returned the Jjimjilbang post
    and then "Categories" and "Tags", which help nobody. Real content only: posts, plus
    the standalone informational pages.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% assign skip_urls = "/search/,/404.html,/journal/,/journal/archive/,/journal/category/,/journal/tag/,/gallery/,/games/,/naver/" | split: "," %}
  {% assign entries = "" | split: "" %}
  {% for post in site.posts %}{% assign entries = entries | push: post %}{% endfor %}
  {% for page in site.pages %}
    {% unless skip_urls contains page.url %}
      {% comment %}
        Paginated journal pages and the per-category/per-tag archives are generated
        listings too; they all live under /journal/page or /journal/category/ or
        /journal/tag/, so a prefix test catches them without listing each one.
      {% endcomment %}
      {% assign is_listing = false %}
      {% if page.url contains '/journal/page' %}{% assign is_listing = true %}{% endif %}
      {% if page.url contains '/journal/category/' %}{% assign is_listing = true %}{% endif %}
      {% if page.url contains '/journal/tag/' %}{% assign is_listing = true %}{% endif %}
      {% comment %}
        `page.title` is compared against "" rather than tested for truthiness: the home
        page carries `title: ""`, and an empty string is truthy in Liquid, so a bare
        `{% raw %}{% if page.title %}{% endraw %}` admitted it and produced an entry
        with a blank label in the results list.
      {% endcomment %}
      {% assign entry_title = page.title | strip %}
      {% if entry_title != "" and is_listing == false %}
        {% assign entries = entries | push: page %}
      {% endif %}
    {% endunless %}
  {% endfor %}
  {% for item in entries %}
  {
    "title": {{ item.title | jsonify }},
    "url": {{ item.url | relative_url | jsonify }},
    "date": {% if item.date %}{{ item.date | date: "%Y-%m-%d" | jsonify }}{% else %}""{% endif %},
    "category": {{ item.categories | join: ", " | jsonify }},
    "tags": {{ item.tags | join: ", " | jsonify }},
    "desc": {{ item.description | default: item.subtitle | default: "" | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | jsonify }},
    "content": {{ item.content | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | truncate: 1200 | jsonify }}
  }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
  {% endfor %}
]
